    "created_at": "2025-10-01T15:13:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-01T15:19:29Z",
    "body": "Yes, I think we should include programmatic scrolling. Not just for user triggered programmatic scrolls as mentioned in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11732#issuecomment-3356568871 but also for cases where the developer intends for something to be scrolled to.\n\nIn particular, if the developer has a call to scroll to some location on the page it shouldn't make a difference whether the site loads quickly or slowly, that location should be scrolled into view without them having to fight the browser scroll restoration. If we didn't include programmatic scrolls then,\n* If the site loads quickly, their scroll applies after, and is respected.\n* If the site loads slowly, their scroll applies before and is overridden by the browser scroll restoration / fragment navigation / scroll start.\n\nIn some cases the developer may know better when / how to scroll the correct content into view - e.g. after some lazy loading / infinite scroll setup.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
