    "created_at": "2025-10-01T15:58:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-01T15:58:27Z",
    "body": "Perhaps the right choice here is to retain a timestamp of when the root scroller is scrolled then, and we can use that as a heuristic to determine if the scroller has been scrolled netween the time the navigate event was fired and the time the scroll should be performed. \n\nI've tried this in Gecko and it seems to work well enough. ",
