    "created_at": "2025-10-08T19:19:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-08T19:19:12Z",
    "body": "@keithamus It seems like that approach would count some scrolls that Chromium currently leaves out, right? For example, Chromium does not count three kinds of scrolling as \"explicit\" scrolls: `kClamping`, `kAnchoring`, and `kScrollStart`, so on a page using CSS scroll start, I'd expect Chrome to override the scroll start position with the restored position, and Gecko to override the restoration itself with the scroll start position.",
